    <section class="word-day" aria-labelledby="word-day">
      <h2 id="word-day">Word of the day</h2>
      <p class="word-greek" lang="grc">ξένος</p>
      <p>
        <em>xenos</em>, the guest, and also the host. Menelaus asks Zeus to punish
        Paris so that later men will shrink from doing ill deeds in the house of a
        host. That is the wrong he thinks the duel is for. Say <em>xenos</em> once.
        You do not need a textbook to keep it.
      </p>
    </section>

